        {"q": "What is the difference between a terminal and a shell?",
         "a": "The terminal is the program that draws the window and passes your keystrokes on. The shell is the program inside it that reads each line, expands globs and variables, and starts other programs. You can run different shells in the same terminal, such as zsh on a Mac and bash over SSH on a server. When a command behaves differently on two machines, look at the shell and the tool versions, not the terminal."},
